  "note": "Triennial election of the Ballycastle Urban District Council due on Wednesday 17 May 1961; it was postponed for a month owing to the death of a candidate and declared on 15 June 1961. Seventeen candidates (twelve Nationalists and five Unionists) contested twelve seats; ten Nationalists and two Unionists were elected (Belfast News-Letter, 17 June 1961, p. 5). Six candidates for five seats."
